>> thank you.

02:20:52.800 --> 02:20:54.800
Supervisor mahmud.

02:20:55.270 --> 02:20:56.370
Supervisor randleman.

02:20:56.370 --> 02:20:58.437
>> thank you, MADAM Clerk.

02:20:59.108 --> 02:20:59.942
Colleagues today I have a few

02:20:59.942 --> 02:21:02.342
behavioral health hearings to

02:21:02.778 --> 02:21:03.746
introduce.

02:21:03.746 --> 02:21:04.513
The first is a hearing on the

02:21:04.513 --> 02:21:06.382
findings and recommendations of

02:21:06.382 --> 02:21:07.150
the residential care

02:21:07.150 --> 02:21:07.783
and treatment workgroup.

02:21:07.783 --> 02:21:10.183
The comptroller's office issued

02:21:11.219 --> 02:21:12.187
this report on JANUARY 7th.

02:21:12.187 --> 02:21:15.624
The final full day of the

02:21:15.624 --> 02:21:16.291
administration.

02:21:16.291 --> 02:21:17.260
>> mayor breed had at my

02:21:17.260 --> 02:21:19.261
request convened the workgroup

02:21:19.261 --> 02:21:19.962
following passage of

02:21:19.962 --> 02:21:22.962
proposition one in MARCH of

02:21:23.320 --> 02:21:23.766
last year to identify capacity

02:21:23.766 --> 02:21:24.433
and placement gaps for people

02:21:24.433 --> 02:21:25.100
with severe mental illness

02:21:25.100 --> 02:21:27.500
in our residential treatment

02:21:27.569 --> 02:21:28.303
portfolio and to develop

02:21:28.303 --> 02:21:30.303
strategic recommendations to

02:21:30.872 --> 02:21:31.673
guide the city's response to

02:21:31.673 --> 02:21:32.307
the dire shortage of long term

02:21:32.307 --> 02:21:34.707
beds for this population.

02:21:35.344 --> 02:21:36.450
The work group's deliberations

02:21:36.450 --> 02:21:36.646
helped lay the foundation for

02:21:36.646 --> 02:21:38.646
the city's application

02:21:39.248 --> 02:21:39.982
in DECEMBER of last year for

02:21:39.982 --> 02:21:42.251
prop one funding to among other

02:21:42.251 --> 02:21:42.885
things allow us to add

02:21:42.885 --> 02:21:43.619
approximately 100 locked

02:21:43.619 --> 02:21:46.619
subacute treatment beds to our

02:21:47.890 --> 02:21:47.823
current portfolio of 140.

02:21:47.823 --> 02:21:50.392
We anticipate hearing from the

02:21:50.392 --> 02:21:50.993
state on the outcome of that

02:21:50.993 --> 02:21:51.761
application imminently.

02:21:51.761 --> 02:21:54.263
Whether or not we receive that

02:21:54.263 --> 02:21:54.964
funding however, the issues

02:21:54.964 --> 02:21:57.364
and strategies considered by

02:21:57.934 --> 02:21:58.634
the workgroup deserve at the

02:21:58.634 --> 02:21:59.335
very least a hearing before a

02:21:59.335 --> 02:21:59.935
committee of this board to

02:21:59.935 --> 02:22:02.335
inform our response to

02:22:02.437 --> 02:22:03.172
california's decades old

02:22:03.172 --> 02:22:05.507
failure to appropriately care

02:22:05.507 --> 02:22:05.975
for indigent people with severe

02:22:05.975 --> 02:22:06.742
mental illness.

02:22:06.742 --> 02:22:07.476
I want to thank public safety

02:22:07.476 --> 02:22:09.876
and neighborhood services chair

02:22:10.413 --> 02:22:12.549
