02:22:19.722 --> 02:22:20.489
of this hearing on that same

02:22:20.489 --> 02:22:21.223
date and at the same committee.

02:22:21.223 --> 02:22:24.193
I'll also be holding a hearing

02:22:24.193 --> 02:22:24.927
on san francisco's

02:22:24.927 --> 02:22:27.327
implementation of senate bill

02:22:27.697 --> 02:22:28.365
43 the legislation enacted

02:22:28.365 --> 02:22:29.132
in OCTOBER 2023 and effect

02:22:29.132 --> 02:22:32.135
and in effect since JANUARY of

02:22:32.135 --> 02:22:32.936
last year updated the standard

02:22:32.936 --> 02:22:35.805
for conservatorship of a person

02:22:35.805 --> 02:22:36.539
who is gravely disabled by

02:22:36.539 --> 02:22:38.939
among other things redefining

02:22:39.409 --> 02:22:40.760
grave disability to include a

02:22:40.760 --> 02:22:42.476
mental health disorder or

02:22:42.945 --> 02:22:43.713
severe substance abuse disorder

02:22:43.713 --> 02:22:46.916
that renders a person unable to

02:22:46.916 --> 02:22:47.617
provide for their food,

02:22:47.617 --> 02:22:48.285
clothing, shelter, necessary

02:22:48.285 --> 02:22:48.618
medical care or personal

02:22:48.618 --> 02:22:50.618
safety.

02:22:51.388 --> 02:22:52.220
The legislation also made it

02:22:52.220 --> 02:22:52.655
easier for courts to use

02:22:52.655 --> 02:22:54.891
medical records to prove

02:22:54.891 --> 02:22:55.258
eligibility in conservatorship

02:22:55.258 --> 02:22:55.925
hearings.

02:22:55.925 --> 02:22:58.325
>> the board of supervisors

02:22:58.695 --> 02:23:01.950
supported sb 43 prior to

02:23:02.266 --> 02:23:03.330
passage and now that's been

02:23:03.330 --> 02:23:03.834
in effect for more than a year.

02:23:03.834 --> 02:23:06.303
I think it's time for a check

02:23:06.303 --> 02:23:07.370
in on how our city departments

02:23:07.370 --> 02:23:09.706
and agencies are using this new

02:23:09.706 --> 02:23:10.574
tool to provide care to people

02:23:10.574 --> 02:23:11.308
who do not know they need it

02:23:11.308 --> 02:23:11.575
and will not voluntarily accept

02:23:11.575 --> 02:23:13.575
it.

02:23:13.777 --> 02:23:14.377
And what challenges they're

02:23:14.377 --> 02:23:16.777
finding in doing that?

02:23:17.480 --> 02:23:18.214
My strong suspicion which I've

02:23:18.214 --> 02:23:18.983
expressed frequently it's all

02:23:18.983 --> 02:23:21.485
about the beds and without the

02:23:21.485 --> 02:23:22.219
right kinds of beds.

02:23:22.219 --> 02:23:24.822
The state legislature can amend

02:23:24.822 --> 02:23:25.556
conservatorship laws ad nauseum

02:23:25.556 --> 02:23:26.357
without significantly expanding

02:23:26.357 --> 02:23:29.920
the number of people we're able

02:23:29.920 --> 02:23:29.393
to move into conservatorship

02:23:29.393 --> 02:23:31.393
care.

02:23:32.896 --> 02:23:33.330
See my prior hearing

02:23:33.330 --> 02:23:33.964
announcement.

02:23:33.964 --> 02:23:36.964
Finally, I'm calling for a

02:23:37.340 --> 02:23:39.434
hearing on fiscal year 20 2320

02:23:39.770 --> 02:23:42.170
and the fiscal year 2023 2024

02:23:42.740 --> 02:23:43.730
treatment on demand annual

02:23:43.730 --> 02:23:43.807
report.

02:23:43.807 --> 02:23:46.207
the 2008 treatment on demand

02:23:47.277 --> 02:23:47.945
act also known as proposition t

02:23:47.945 --> 02:23:50.345
